    <main id="content" tabindex="-1">
      <h1>Installing a fixture plugin</h1>
      <p>A server installs plugins from a catalogue it is told about, and the address of that catalogue is a value this page reads rather than a sentence written into it.</p>
      <p>The address is https://fixture.example/manifest.json. It is added once, in the server&#39;s administration pages under the plugin catalogues, and it keeps answering afterwards: what is published under it is what the server sees the next time it looks.</p>
      <p>The list below is computed from what each fixture repository has published, so the page and the table it is reached from are one read of the same file.</p>
      <h2>What can be installed today</h2>
      <p>One of the 6 plugins has a finished release published, so it is the one a server can install today. The rest appear here as they publish, and this list is computed from what each repository has published rather than written on this page.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/plugins/declared-shell-and-shipping/">declared-shell-and-shipping</a> A row declaring the shell state for a repository that has published a finished release, which is the disagreement the state is computed to settle Published for Jellyfin 10.11 and 12.0.</li>
      </ul>
